IMPORT prelude

-- Exchange Control Act 1953 (Singapore) -- what the Act forbids or requires of a person or business without the Monetary
-- Authority's permission: the meaning of "gold", "foreign currency" and the scheduled territories (s 2, First Schedule), dealing
-- in gold and foreign currency (s 3(1)), surrender of gold and specified currency (s 4), payments to persons resident outside the
-- scheduled territories (s 7), the personal representative's residence (s 42(1)), import and export of gold and documents
-- (ss 23, 24), payment for exports (s 25(1), (2)), exemption orders (s 33), the implied condition in contracts (s 35(1), (2)),
-- claims in insolvency (Fourth Schedule para 5), and the offence, penalties and composition (Fifth Schedule Part 2 paras 1, 3, 5).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to and including 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021),
-- informal consolidation, version in force from 1/4/2022, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ECA1953.txt. The latest
-- amendment annotated in the text is Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022 (Fourth Schedule para 3).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0071 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions a person or business meets when holding, buying, paying or carrying money and
-- gold across the border. Not encoded: travellers' cheques (s 6), compensation deals (s 9), the securities provisions of Part 4
-- (ss 10 to 22), debts, goods and settlements (ss 26 to 32), blocked accounts (s 34, Third Schedule), the enforcement powers of
-- Fifth Schedule Parts 1 and 3, and the Second Schedule (foreign companies).
--
-- THE DEPOSIT CONTAINS NO EXEMPTION ORDER, NO ORDER SPECIFYING CURRENCY (s 4(2)), AND NO ORDER PRESCRIBING EXPORT TERRITORIES
-- (s 25(1)). Every prohibition below is subject to s 33 exemptions, modelled as a flag. Whether any of it bites today depends on
-- orders that were not retrieved; this encoding says what the Act's own text does, not what is enforced.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Exchange Control Act 1953 -- currency and payments`

§§ `2 and First Schedule -- scheduled territories and foreign currency`

-- s 2(1): "scheduled territories" means the territories specified in the First Schedule (amendable by order of the Authority).
-- The First Schedule includes Australia, Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China, India,
-- Indonesia, Malaysia, the Philippines, "Singapore, the Republic of", Thailand and "United Kingdom, the Channel Islands and the
-- Isle of Man". It does not list the United States, Japan or Switzerland (nor China beyond the Hong Kong SAR).
DECLARE Territory IS ONE OF
    Singapore
    Malaysia
    `the United Kingdom`
    Australia
    `Hong Kong`
    India
    Indonesia
    Thailand
    `the Philippines`
    `the United States`
    Japan
    Switzerland

GIVEN `the territory` IS A Territory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a scheduled territory` IF
    CONSIDER `the territory`
    WHEN `the United States` THEN FALSE
    WHEN Japan THEN FALSE
    WHEN Switzerland THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 2(1): "foreign currency" "does not include local currency or any currency or notes issued under the law of any part of the
-- scheduled territories". "gold" means gold coin and bullion "and includes any gold in whatever state or form other than gold
-- which has been materially increased in value by skilled craftsmanship".
DECLARE Asset IS ONE OF
    `gold bullion`
    `gold coins`
    `a gold necklace worth much more than its gold for the craftsmanship`
    `Singapore dollars`
    `Malaysian ringgit`
    `pounds sterling`
    `Australian dollars`
    `Hong Kong dollars`
    `US dollars`
    `Japanese yen`
    `Swiss francs`

GIVEN `the asset` IS AN Asset
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is gold` IF
    CONSIDER `the asset`
    WHEN `gold bullion` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `gold coins` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the asset` IS AN Asset
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is foreign currency` IF
    CONSIDER `the asset`
    WHEN `Singapore dollars` THEN NOT `is a scheduled territory` Singapore
    WHEN `Malaysian ringgit` THEN NOT `is a scheduled territory` Malaysia
    WHEN `pounds sterling` THEN NOT `is a scheduled territory` `the United Kingdom`
    WHEN `Australian dollars` THEN NOT `is a scheduled territory` Australia
    WHEN `Hong Kong dollars` THEN NOT `is a scheduled territory` `Hong Kong`
    WHEN `US dollars` THEN NOT `is a scheduled territory` `the United States`
    WHEN `Japanese yen` THEN NOT `is a scheduled territory` Japan
    WHEN `Swiss francs` THEN NOT `is a scheduled territory` Switzerland
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the asset` IS AN Asset
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is gold or foreign currency` IF
    `is gold` `the asset` OR `is foreign currency` `the asset`

§§ `3(1) -- dealing in gold and foreign currency`

-- s 3(1): "Except with the permission of the Authority, no person, other than an authorised dealer, shall in Singapore buy or
-- borrow any gold or foreign currency from, or sell or lend any gold or foreign currency to, any person other than an authorised
-- dealer." s 33(1): every obligation or prohibition has effect "subject to such exemptions as may be granted by order".
DECLARE Deal HAS
    `the asset dealt in` IS AN Asset
    `takes place in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is an authorised dealer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other party is an authorised dealer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Authority permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an exemption order covers it` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the deal` IS A Deal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deal breaches section 3(1)` IF
        `the deal`'s `takes place in Singapore`
    AND `is gold or foreign currency` (`the deal`'s `the asset dealt in`)
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `the person is an authorised dealer`)
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `the other party is an authorised dealer`)
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `the Authority permitted it`)
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `an exemption order covers it`)

§§ `4 -- surrender of gold and specified currency`

-- s 4(1): every person in Singapore entitled to sell gold or specified currency, and not an authorised dealer, "shall offer it, or
-- cause it to be offered, for sale to an authorised dealer, unless the Authority consents to his retention and use thereof or he
-- disposes thereof to any other person with the permission of the Authority". (2): specified currency is "such foreign currency
-- ... as may from time to time be specified by order". (3): if the consent was for a stated purpose and the purpose has
-- ended, (1) applies "as if the Authority had revoked its consent". (4): a person who acquires gold or specified currency from
-- an authorised dealer is treated as having the Authority's consent, and his stated purpose as made in an application for it.
-- (6): on non-compliance the Authority may direct that it vest in the Authority.
DECLARE Holding HAS
    `the asset held` IS AN Asset
    `the holder is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder is entitled to sell it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder is an authorised dealer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the currency is specified by order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Authority consented to retention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was acquired from an authorised dealer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stated purpose has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disposed of with permission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an exemption order covers the holding` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consent to retain is in effect` IF
        (    `the holding`'s `the Authority consented to retention`
         OR  `the holding`'s `it was acquired from an authorised dealer`)
    AND (NOT `the holding`'s `the stated purpose has ended`)

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holder must offer it to an authorised dealer` IF
        `the holding`'s `the holder is in Singapore`
    AND `the holding`'s `the holder is entitled to sell it`
    AND (    `is gold` (`the holding`'s `the asset held`)
         OR  (`is foreign currency` (`the holding`'s `the asset held`) AND `the holding`'s `the currency is specified by order`))
    AND (NOT `the holding`'s `the holder is an authorised dealer`)
    AND (NOT `consent to retain is in effect` `the holding`)
    AND (NOT `the holding`'s `disposed of with permission`)
    AND (NOT `the holding`'s `an exemption order covers the holding`)

§§ `7 and 42(1) -- payments in Singapore`

-- s 7(1): "Except with the permission of the Authority, no person shall do any of the following things in Singapore: (a) make any
-- payment to or for the credit of a person resident outside the scheduled territories; (b) make any payment to or for the credit
-- of a person resident in the scheduled territories by order or on behalf of a person resident outside the scheduled
-- territories; (c) place any sum to the credit of any person resident outside the scheduled territories."
-- The Act forbids the payment whatever its currency: s 7 is not limited to foreign currency.
DECLARE Payment HAS
    `made in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payee resides in` IS A Territory
    `made on the order of a person resident in` IS A Territory
    `the Authority permitted the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an exemption order covers the payment` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment breaches section 7(1)` IF
        `the payment`'s `made in Singapore`
    AND (    (NOT `is a scheduled territory` (`the payment`'s `the payee resides in`))
         OR  (NOT `is a scheduled territory` (`the payment`'s `made on the order of a person resident in`)))
    AND (NOT `the payment`'s `the Authority permitted the payment`)
    AND (NOT `the payment`'s `an exemption order covers the payment`)

-- s 42(1): a personal representative "shall, unless the Authority otherwise directs, be treated as resident in the territory where
-- the deceased person was resident ... at the time of his death and as not resident elsewhere, so far as relates to any matters in
-- which the personal representative is concerned solely in his capacity as such".
GIVEN `own residence` IS A Territory, `the deceased's residence` IS A Territory, `acting solely as personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Authority otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Territory
`the personal representative's residence for the Act` MEANS
    IF `acting solely as personal representative` AND (NOT `the Authority otherwise directs`)
    THEN `the deceased's residence`
    ELSE `own residence`

§§ `23 and 24 -- import and export`

-- s 23(1): no person shall import into Singapore without permission (a) notes specified by order of the Authority; (b) "any
-- Treasury bills"; (c) "any certificate of title to any security", including cancelled ones. Gold is NOT in s 23.
-- s 24: no person shall export without permission (a) "any postal orders"; (b) "any Treasury bills"; (c) "any gold"; (d)(i) any
-- certificate of title to a security and any coupon; (ii) "any policy of assurance"; (iii) "any bill of exchange or promissory note
-- expressed in terms of a currency other than that of a scheduled territory and payable otherwise than within the scheduled
-- territories"; (f) articles on a traveller or in baggage "as may be prescribed".
-- s 2(1): "securities" includes shares and units under a unit trust scheme; "policy of assurance" includes a policy assuring money
-- on death (except death by accident only).
DECLARE Article IS ONE OF
    `gold bars`
    `a gold necklace of fine craftsmanship`
    `a postal order`
    `a Treasury bill`
    `a share certificate`
    `a whole-life insurance policy`
    `a promissory note in US dollars payable in New York`
    `a promissory note in ringgit payable in Kuala Lumpur`
    `a promissory note in US dollars payable in Singapore`
    `Singapore banknotes`
    `a laptop`

GIVEN `the article` IS AN Article
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `importing it needs permission under section 23` IF
    CONSIDER `the article`
    WHEN `a Treasury bill` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a share certificate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the article` IS AN Article
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exporting it needs permission under section 24` IF
    CONSIDER `the article`
    WHEN `gold bars` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a postal order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Treasury bill` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a share certificate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a whole-life insurance policy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a promissory note in US dollars payable in New York` THEN
            NOT `is a scheduled territory` `the United States`
    WHEN `a promissory note in ringgit payable in Kuala Lumpur` THEN NOT `is a scheduled territory` Malaysia
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `25(1), (2) -- payment for exports`

-- s 25(1): no person shall without permission export goods to a destination in a prescribed territory "unless the Authority is
-- satisfied -- (a) that payment for the goods has been made to a person resident in Singapore in such manner as may be prescribed
-- ..., or is to be so made not later than 6 months after the date of exportation; and (b) that the amount ... represent[s] a return
-- for the goods which is in all the circumstances in accordance with the objects of this Act". (2): the Authority may direct a
-- longer or shorter period for (a), or omit the deferred-payment words altogether (modelled as a period of 0 months).
DECLARE `Export Sale` HAS
    `the destination is in a prescribed territory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Authority permitted the export` IS A BOOLEAN
    `already paid to a Singapore resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months after exportation payment is due` IS A NUMBER
    `a direction substitutes a period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the substituted period in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the return accords with the objects of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the sale` IS AN `Export Sale`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment period in months` MEANS
    IF `the sale`'s `a direction substitutes a period` THEN `the sale`'s `the substituted period in months` ELSE 6

GIVEN `the sale` IS AN `Export Sale`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the export may proceed under section 25` IF
        (NOT `the sale`'s `the destination is in a prescribed territory`)
    OR  `the sale`'s `the Authority permitted the export`
    OR  (    (    `the sale`'s `already paid to a Singapore resident`
              OR  `the sale`'s `months after exportation payment is due` AT MOST `the payment period in months` `the sale`)
         AND `the sale`'s `the return accords with the objects of the Act`)

§§ `35(1), (2) and Fourth Schedule para 5 -- contracts and insolvency`

-- s 35(1): "It shall be an implied condition in any contract that, where, by virtue of this Act, the permission or consent of the
-- Authority is at the time of the contract required for the performance of any term thereof, that term shall not be performed
-- except insofar as the permission or consent is given or is not required." (2): not "insofar as it is shown to be inconsistent
-- with the intention of the parties".
GIVEN `permission required at the time of contract` IS A BOOLEAN, `permission given` IS A BOOLEAN, `shown inconsistent with the parties' intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the implied condition holds back performance` IF
        `permission required at the time of contract`
    AND (NOT `permission given`)
    AND (NOT `shown inconsistent with the parties' intention`)

-- Fourth Schedule para 5(1): in a Singapore bankruptcy, winding up or administration of an estate, a claim for a sum not payable
-- without permission "shall, notwithstanding that the permission has not been given or has been revoked, be admitted to proof as
-- if it had been given". (2): Part 3 still applies to payments by the trustee, liquidator or personal representative.
GIVEN `permission needed for the sum` IS A BOOLEAN, `permission granted for the sum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is admitted to proof` IF TRUE

GIVEN `permission needed for the sum` IS A BOOLEAN, `permission granted for the sum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trustee may pay the claim without more` IF
    (NOT `permission needed for the sum`) OR `permission granted for the sum`

§§ `Fifth Schedule Part 2 -- offences and penalties`

-- Part 2 para 1(1): "Any person in or resident in Singapore who contravenes or fails to comply with any restriction or requirement"
-- under the Act, or conspires, attempts, aids, abets, counsels or procures, is guilty of an offence. (3): "a fine not exceeding
-- $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or ... both", with discretionary forfeiture. (5): where the offence
-- relates to currency, securities, a payment, gold, goods or other property and "does not consist only of a failure to give
-- information or produce" documents, "the maximum fine ... shall be such fine as is authorised by sub-paragraph (3) or a fine equal
-- to 3 times the value". READ HERE (an inference: the text does not say "whichever is greater") as the greater of the two.
-- s 2(7): the Act's obligations "apply to all persons notwithstanding that they are not in Singapore and are not citizens".
GIVEN `in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `can commit a Part 2 offence` IF
    `in Singapore` OR `resident in Singapore`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `concerns property` IS A BOOLEAN, `only a failure to give information` IS A BOOLEAN, `value of the property` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `concerns property` AND (NOT `only a failure to give information`)
    THEN `the larger of` 10000 (3 TIMES `value of the property`)
    ELSE 10000

`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS 3

-- Part 2 para 3(1): the Authority "may compound any offence ... by accepting ... a sum of money not exceeding $1,000"; (2) on
-- payment, seized property "shall be released and no further proceedings shall be taken".
GIVEN `the sum offered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sum may be accepted in composition` IF
    `the sum offered` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the sum offered` AT MOST 1000

-- Part 2 para 5(1): "No proceedings for an offence punishable under this Part shall be instituted, except with the consent of the
-- Attorney-General or the Authority." (2): against a principal or employer for an agent's act, only with the Attorney-General's
-- consent.
GIVEN `against an employer for an employee's act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Attorney-General consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Authority consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proceedings may be instituted` IF
    IF `against an employer for an employee's act`
    THEN `the Attorney-General consented`
    ELSE `the Attorney-General consented` OR `the Authority consented`
